Change-Id: plvunrqwxwxvkzqwyzlxzvnvuxlzvssr

process-email replied only to the sender, so every answer went to Pat
alone and the list never saw it. The list is the record of the work:
anyone reading lab-devel missed the replies, and threads there looked
unanswered.

Reply-all is the convention on the lists we resemble. The Linux
kernel's etiquette says to always reply-all unless there is good
reason not to, and Git, PostgreSQL, and FreeBSD say the same. Pat
writes to lab-devel@p7x.dev, so a reply-all reaches him and the list.

A message sent to one person directly would still leave the list out,
so the skill adds the list to Cc whenever it is missing.
